---
// src/pages/share/wy-roadless-areas/sources.astro
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Wyoming Roadless Areas — Sources & Background | Skovgard 2026"
  description="Source links and neutral background for the Wyoming Roadless Areas Survey. Official sources, bill text, and Wyoming public-interest perspectives."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="pt-20">

    <!-- Breadcrumb bar -->
    <div class="bg-wy-bone border-b border-gray-200 py-3 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
        <a href="/share" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest transition-colors shrink-0">
          <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
          </svg>
          All messages
        </a>
        <span class="text-gray-300 text-sm">/</span>
        <a href="/share/wy-roadless-areas/" class="text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400 hover:text-wy-ember transition-colors truncate">
          Wyoming Roadless Areas Survey
        </a>
        <span class="text-gray-300 text-sm">/</span>
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-wy-charcoal">Sources</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Page header -->
    <div class="bg-wy-charcoal py-12 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p class="text-wy-sandstone font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-xs mb-3">Research Aid</p>
        <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif font-extrabold text-wy-bone mb-4 leading-tight">
          Wyoming Roadless Areas Survey<br />
          <span class="text-wy-sandstone">Sources &amp; Background</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-wy-bone/75 text-base leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
          These links are provided for voters who want to review the source material. Source review
          is optional and is not required to answer the survey. The questions are intended to measure
          opinion, not persuade.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Preamble -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="preamble-box">
          <p class="preamble-label">Research aid — not a legal opinion</p>
          <p class="preamble-text">
            This page is a research aid for Wyoming voters. It pairs claims made in the survey
            context with their primary sources. Links go to official federal sources, enrolled
            legislation, and Wyoming public-interest organizations. Do not treat this page as
            legal advice, policy advocacy, or a complete account of any ongoing proceeding.
            Use the sources to form your own view.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Why this survey -->
    <section class="bg-white py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="sources-h2">Why this survey was created</h2>
        <p class="body-prose">
          Wyoming has more than 3 million acres of inventoried roadless areas on National Forest
          System lands. A current federal rulemaking process is considering rescission of the 2001
          Roadless Rule, and H.R.&nbsp;7695 would make the 2001 rule have no force or effect while
          requiring certain permanent and temporary roads where deemed necessary. This creates a
          timely Wyoming question: what standards should guide our voice before decisions are made?
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Neutral background -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="sources-h2">Short neutral background</h2>
        <p class="body-prose">
          The 2001 Roadless Rule generally limited new road construction, road reconstruction,
          and timber harvest in inventoried roadless areas, with limited exceptions.
        </p>
        <p class="body-prose">
          USDA and the Forest Service argue that rescission would return more decision-making to
          local land managers and improve flexibility for wildfire risk, forest health, timber work,
          and rural economies.
        </p>
        <p class="body-prose">
          Conservation and recreation groups argue that roadless protections help protect water,
          wildlife habitat, backcountry hunting and fishing, recreation, solitude, and long-term
          public-land inheritance.
        </p>
        <p class="body-prose">
          The survey asks Wyoming voters to weigh these values and choose standards for decision-making.
        </p>

        <h3 class="sources-h3">Key distinctions</h3>
        <ul class="key-distinctions">
          <li>Inventoried roadless area is not the same as congressionally designated Wilderness.</li>
          <li>A temporary road is intended for a limited project or emergency purpose; a permanent road remains for long-term use.</li>
          <li>Rule changes do not automatically approve every project. Project-level review, forest plans, laws, and public process can still matter.</li>
          <li>The public question is not only protection versus development. It is also about water, fire, access, wildlife, costs, accountability, and local judgment.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Claims and sources table -->
    <section class="bg-white py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="sources-h2">Claims and source support</h2>

        <div class="sources-table">

          <div class="source-row">
            <div class="source-claim">Wyoming has more than 3 million acres of inventoried roadless areas on National Forest System lands.</div>
            <div class="source-backing">
              <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/managing-land/planning/roadless/state-maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
                USDA Forest Service — Roadless Areas by State
              </a>
              <span class="source-note">Official state acreage summaries and map links, including Wyoming.</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="source-row">
            <div class="source-claim">A current federal rulemaking process is considering rescission of the 2001 Roadless Rule.</div>
            <div class="source-backing">
              <a href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/08/29/2025-16581/special-areas-roadless-area-conservation-national-forest-system-lands" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
                Federal Register — Special Areas; Roadless Area Conservation; National Forest System Lands (Aug. 29, 2025)
              </a>
              <span class="source-note">Official notice of intent, public-comment timeline, purpose, proposed action, and issues for review.</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="source-row">
            <div class="source-claim">The 2001 Roadless Rule generally limited new road construction, road reconstruction, and timber harvest in inventoried roadless areas, with limited exceptions.</div>
            <div class="source-backing">
              <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/managing-land/planning/roadless" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
                USDA Forest Service — Roadless Areas overview
              </a>
              <span class="source-note">Official overview of the 2001 rule, current rulemaking status, and GIS/map resources.</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="source-row">
            <div class="source-claim">USDA announced rescission of the Roadless Rule on June 23, 2025, citing management flexibility and wildfire risk.</div>
            <div class="source-backing">
              <a href="https://www.usda.gov/about-usda/news/press-releases/2025/06/23/secretary-rollins-rescinds-roadless-rule-eliminating-impediment-responsible-forestmanagement" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
                USDA — June 23, 2025 press release
              </a>
              <span class="source-note">Agency statement explaining the management-flexibility and wildfire-risk argument for rescission.</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="source-row">
            <div class="source-claim">USDA Forest Service opened public comment and an environmental impact statement process on August 27, 2025.</div>
            <div class="source-backing">
              <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/about-agency/newsroom/releases/usda-opens-next-step-roadless-rule-rescission" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
                USDA Forest Service — August 27, 2025 announcement
              </a>
              <span class="source-note">Agency statement announcing public comment and the environmental impact statement process.</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="source-row">
            <div class="source-claim">H.R. 7695 would make the 2001 rule have no force or effect while requiring certain permanent and temporary roads where deemed necessary.</div>
            <div class="source-backing">
              <a href="https://docs.house.gov/meetings/II/II10/20260521/119263/BILLS-119HR7695ih.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="source-link">
                H.R. 7695 bill text (119th Congress)
              </a>
              <span class="source-note">Bill text addressing nullification of the 2001 rule and required road construction language.</span>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Official sources -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="sources-h2">Official sources</h2>

        <div class="link-list">
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/managing-land/planning/roadless" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              USDA Forest Service — Roadless Areas
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Official overview of the 2001 Roadless Rule, current rulemaking status, and GIS/map resources.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2025/08/29/2025-16581/special-areas-roadless-area-conservation-national-forest-system-lands" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              Federal Register — Special Areas; Roadless Area Conservation; National Forest System Lands
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Official notice of intent, public-comment timeline, purpose, proposed action, and issues for review.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/managing-land/planning/roadless/state-maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              USDA Forest Service — Roadless Areas by State
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Official state acreage summaries and map links, including Wyoming.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://www.fs.usda.gov/sites/default/files/roadless-map-wyoming-high-resolution-fsmrs-072382.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              USDA Forest Service — Wyoming Roadless Areas Map (PDF)
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Printable map showing Wyoming inventoried roadless areas on National Forest System lands.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://docs.house.gov/meetings/II/II10/20260521/119263/BILLS-119HR7695ih.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              H.R. 7695 bill text (119th Congress)
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Bill text addressing nullification of the 2001 rule and required road construction language.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Wyoming and public-interest sources -->
    <section class="bg-white py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="sources-h2">Wyoming and public-interest sources</h2>
        <p class="body-prose sources-note">
          The following sources represent a range of perspectives. Inclusion here does not
          constitute endorsement by Skovgard for Senate.
        </p>

        <div class="link-list">
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://www.wildwyo.org/maps" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              Wyoming Wilderness Association — Maps
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Includes a roadless areas interactive map and conservation-focused explanation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://wyomingoutdoorcouncil.org/2025/09/03/roadless-rule/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              Wyoming Outdoor Council — Roadless Rule
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Protection-focused Wyoming discussion of roadless-area values and concerns.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://greateryellowstone.org/roadless-rule" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              Greater Yellowstone Coalition — Roadless Rule
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Protection-focused regional discussion of roadless lands in the Greater Yellowstone area.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://blueribboncoalition.org/usda-accepting-comments-on-roadless-rule-rescission-support-this-win-for-public-land-access/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              BlueRibbon Coalition — Roadless Rule rescission
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Access and management-flexibility focused discussion supporting rescission.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="link-entry">
            <a href="https://www.uwyo.edu/law/centers/center-for-land-and-water-law/blog/long-road-rescinding-roadless-rule.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link-title">
              University of Wyoming College of Law — The Long Road to Rescinding the Roadless Rule
            </a>
            <p class="link-desc">Legal-process overview of rescission, NEPA, consultation, public comment, and litigation risk.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Questions to consider -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="sources-h2">Questions to consider while reading</h2>
        <ul class="key-distinctions">
          <li>Which areas are Wilderness, which are inventoried roadless areas, and which are other public lands?</li>
          <li>Which proposed actions would use temporary roads, and which would create permanent roads?</li>
          <li>What water, wildlife, fire, access, and cost information should be published before a decision?</li>
          <li>How should Wyoming voices be gathered, reported, and compared with future decisions?</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Responsible use note -->
    <section class="bg-white py-10 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <div class="use-note-box">
          <p class="use-note-label">Notes for responsible use</p>
          <ul class="use-note-list">
            <li>The rulemaking process involves ongoing agency action, public comment, and potential litigation. Check official sources for current status before citing.</li>
            <li>H.R. 7695 is federal legislation introduced in the 119th Congress. Its current status should be verified against official congressional records before citing as passed or enacted.</li>
            <li>Distinguish between what the rule says, what agencies claim about the rule, and what courts have held. These are not always the same.</li>
            <li>Results from this survey represent participating voters only. They are not a scientific sample of Wyoming public opinion.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Back CTA -->
    <section class="bg-wy-bone py-12 px-4">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center">
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-6">
          Ready to take the survey or share it with Wyoming neighbors?
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3">
          <a
            href="https://grassrootsmvt.org/surveys/wy-roadless-areas"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-wy-ember text-wy-bone font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-wy-ember-dark transition-colors text-sm shadow"
          >
            Take the Survey
          </a>
          <a
            href="/share/wy-roadless-areas/"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 bg-wy-charcoal text-wy-bone font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-wy-ember-dark transition-colors text-sm"
          >
            Share the survey
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .body-prose {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  .sources-note {
    color: #6b7280;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .sources-h2 {
    font-family: 'Bitter', serif;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #e5ddd0;
  }
  .sources-h3 {
    font-family: 'Bitter', serif;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    margin: 24px 0 10px;
  }

  /* Preamble */
  .preamble-box {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid #e5ddd0;
    border-left: 4px solid #7a8a6b;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .preamble-label {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #7a8a6b;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .preamble-text {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #4b4b4b;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Key distinctions list */
  .key-distinctions {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .key-distinctions li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2b2b2b;
  }
  .key-distinctions li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 9px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    background: #c68a4a;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  /* Claims and sources table */
  .sources-table {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid #e5ddd0;
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .source-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5ddd0;
  }
  .source-row:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .source-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
  .source-claim {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #2b2b2b;
    background: #f9f6f0;
    border-right: 1px solid #e5ddd0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .source-claim { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5ddd0; }
  }
  .source-backing {
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .source-link {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #0f2742;
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .source-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-note {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: #6b7280;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  /* Link list */
  .link-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .link-entry { }
  .link-title {
    display: inline;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #0f2742;
    text-decoration: none;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .link-title:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .link-desc {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: #4b4b4b;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 3px 0 0;
  }

  /* Responsible use note */
  .use-note-box {
    background: #f9f6f0;
    border: 1px solid #e5ddd0;
    border-left: 4px solid #c68a4a;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
  }
  .use-note-label {
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: #7a8a6b;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .use-note-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .use-note-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 18px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #4b4b4b;
  }
  .use-note-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 8px;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    background: #7a8a6b;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
</style>
